ADDENDA <Act No. 7142, Jan. 29, 2004>
Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Transitional Measures concerning Korea Network Information Center)
(1) The incorporated foundation, Korea Network Information Center (hereinafter referred to as the "Information Center") may apply for approval for the succession of its rights and duties to the Minister of Information and Communication, at the time when this Act enters into force, to ensure that its rights and obligations are succeeded by the Korea Internet and Security Agency established under Article 9, after undergoing the resolution of the board of directors.
(2) The Information Center, which has obtained approval by making an application under paragraph (1), shall be deemed dissolved, when the Internet and Security Agency under this Act is established, notwithstanding the provisions on the dissolution or liquidation of incorporated foundations in the Civil Act, and all properties, rights and obligations belonging to the Information Center shall be succeeded by the Internet and Security Agency established under this Act.
(3) Employees of the Information Center, at the time this Act enters into force, shall be deemed employees of the Internet and Security Agency, from the date on which the Information Center receives approval from the Minister of Information and Communication under paragraph (1).
Article 3 (Transitional Measures concerning Internet Addresses)
Internet protocol addresses assigned by the Information Center or domain names registered with the Information Center, at the time this Act enters into force, shall be deemed Internet protocol addresses assigned by Internet address management organizations or domain names registered with Internet address management organizations under this Act, respectively.
Article 4 Omitted.

